    "result_text": "I added `get_account_by_email_ci` to `lnbits/core/crud/users.py`, just above `get_account_by_pubkey`. I haven't run the function or any tests.\n\nIt's based on the catalog pattern `crud.get_account_by_field@v1`, with the `# pcat:` marker kept above it. The pattern looks accounts up by username, so I changed it to match on `LOWER(email)` and renamed the parameter to `email`. Like the sibling lookups, it:\n- returns `None` for an empty email;\n- lowercases the input before comparing;\n- only returns activated accounts unless you pass `active_only=False`;\n- takes an optional `conn`.\n\n`check_code` found no high-severity deviations and nothing needing human approval. It flagged two low-severity differences, which come from the username-to-email change.\n\nThe lookup compares `LOWER(email)` in the query, so it won't use a plain index on `email`. The existing `get_account_by_username_or_email` already queries that way."
